{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277882-two-artifacts-winter-lightning-zapatos-dancer-s-boots-white-elephant-for-valles","id":1277882,"title":"Two artifacts: Winter Lightning & Zapatos, Dancer's Boots (White Elephant for Valles)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-01T11:47:30-08:00","id":1277882,"title":"Two artifacts: Winter Lightning & Zapatos, Dancer's Boots (White Elephant for Valles)","content":"I wrote two artifacts to serve as signature heirlooms for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar280_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"280\" data-vbnamecard=\"280\">Valles</a> Dragon-blooded characters. Since they are tailor-made for particular characters, I haven't bothered writing Resonant or Dissonant effects for any of the Evocations. Happy holidays! I hope these are to your liking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Winter Lightning, the Duelist\u2019s Steel (Blue jade Reaper Daiklave, 4-dot artifact)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stories of the Winter Lightning, a fabled dueling blade forged from a rare alloy of steel and Blue jade, range from utterly mundane to absolutely fantastical. What is common between the stories is that the Winter Lighting appears time to time in the hands of famous history\u2019s famous duelists. The sword seems to crave recognition and it is especially drawn to tales of revenge, whether they are stories of just retribution or bloody fulfilling of a vendetta.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The actual blade is an azure-blue Reaper Daiklave that seems to fizzle with barely contained energy. Touching the blade means submitting to dozens of small electrical shocks, which discourage idle hands. Even if those attuned to the blade describe them as fairly comforting. It is said that during a storm the wielders of the blade seek battle or risk the sword\u2019s volatile energy hurting anyone unfortunate enough to be near when the static charge overloads.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But regardless of whether you believe the tales or not, witnessing the Winter Lightning duel is a sight treasured - or feared - for the rest of one\u2019s lifespan. The duellers become almost magnetic as the blade\u2019s will draws them together to complete their battle. In the aftermath, there is usually not much left of the loser. And the sword only remembers the victorious.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of the Winter Lightning</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those attuned to the Winter Lightning may designate a foe as their nemesis at the start of the battle. They do not suffer onslaught penalties from attacks made by their nemesis and additionally they may add a relevant Intimacy as non-charm bonus dice to any attack roll they make against their nemesis. However, those dissonant with the artifact must apply the same Intimacy as a penalty if they are attacking any other foe, as long as their nemesis still stands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attunement: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5m</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium (as Reaper daiklave)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lethal, Melee, Balanced</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heartstone slots: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Era: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Age of Dreams</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lightning Edge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By channeling her essence through the Winter Lighting, the blade\u2019s wielder is able to charge her weapon with electricity. When she hits an enemy, this current is released. When hitting an enemy with a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering attack, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the wielder may ignore a point of armor soak for every 10 in their attack roll. When hitting an enemy with a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack, the wielder may turn one of her damage dice into an automatic success for every level of armour the enemy has (one for light armour, two for medium armour, three for heavy armour).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Evocation awakens at no cost, when the Winter Lightning is first attuned.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cobalt Flash</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every strike of Winter Lighting is a thunderbolt, every battle a storm. Electricity, barely contained, is released as a blinding flash when the blade strikes steel. This evocation can be activated when an enemy hits the wielder with an attack. For every 1 result in enemy\u2019s roll, they suffer one die penalty (up to the wielder\u2019s Essence) to their actions until the end of their next round. If the attack comes from the wielder\u2019s nemesis, the penalty affects every foe engaged with the wielder.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rebuking Shock</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: - Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Cobalt Flash, Flame-borne Interception</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Winter Lightning parries an attack, the static charge inside burst as a deadly shower of sparks. This evocation </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">upgrades </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">its prerequisite by increasing the parry by two instead of one, when parrying an attack by the wielder\u2019s nemesis.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, if the wielder parries an attack by an enemy other than the nemesis, the enemy suffers one die of Initiative damage. This damage bypasses soak and does not increase the wielder\u2019s Initiative.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duel-Forcing Lunge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous, Withering-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Lightning Edge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Winter Lightning is a honorable blade and it hates to see its foe ignore a duel. This evocation allows the wielder to reflexively move and make a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">clash attack against the wielder\u2019s nemesis, if the foe tries to attack someone other than the wielder. This counts as the wielder\u2019s action this round (or the next, if they have already acted this round).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This evocation can only be used once per scene unless it is reset by Initiative crashing the wielder\u2019s nemesis.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fulcrum Doppelg\u00e4nger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Lightning Edge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those dueling against the Winter Lightning sometimes feel they are facing multiple opponents. This evocation allows the wielder to create an after-image of crackling electricity. This image lasts for rounds equal to (1 + the wielder\u2019s Essence). Each after-image raises the wielder\u2019s Evasion by +2. If an enemy misses an attack against the wielder by this margin, the after-image disappears and deals (the wielder\u2019s Essence) dice of Initiative damage to the enemy. These dice bypass Soak.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the Evocation Thunderbolt Arena is active, the activation cost of Fulcrum Doppelg\u00e4nger is reduced to 1 mote.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thunderclap Assist</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3+m, 1wp Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Fulcrum Doppelg\u00e4nger</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the wielder\u2019s relationship with Winter Lightning develops, she realizes that the after-images created by the blade do not follow her movements, but her intent. A skilled wielder is thus able to direct them towards different tasks. This Evocation supplements a flurry. The wielder pays a point of Willpower and 3 motes for every doppelg\u00e4nger they want to assist in the flurry.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For each doppelg\u00e4nger activated by this evocation one action can be flurried without the usual flurry penalty with the after-image performing the action instead of the wielder. The after-images vanish after performing their action. This Evocation can be used to flurry actions that normally cannot be flurried, such as performing a shape sorcery action or attacking more times than once. However, the after-images can only perform </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attacks and even then their Initiative damage does not add to the wielder\u2019s Initiative.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While the Evocation Thunderbolt Arena is active, the Willpower only needs to be paid once per scene, not once per activation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crackling Affondo</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Thunderclap Assist</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A faint spark draws a course between the Winter Lightning and its target\u2019s heart, creating a way for the current to travel. This is a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive attack</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> targeting the wielder\u2019s designated nemesis. Any engaged after-images may target and attack the nemesis with the wielder dividing her Initiative pool evenly between herself and the after-images. For every doppelg\u00e4nger that hits, the wielder may turn one of her damage dice into an automatic success. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thunderbolt Arena</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m, 1wp Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Crackling Affondo</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By raising the Winter Lighting, the wielder challenges Heaven itself to witness a duel between two arch-enemies. The Blade crackles with lightning and when the wielder swirls it around, the energy draws a crackling boundary on the ground that isolates the wielder and her nemesis from rest of the battle.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This lightning boundary lasts until either of the combatants, the wielder or her nemesis, lay incapacitated on the ground. Anyone trying to cross the boundary (in or out) must succeed in a (Stamina + Resistance) test against difficulty of (the wielder\u2019s Essence), or they are hurled back and suffer (the wielder\u2019s Essence) dice of lethal damage. Even if they succeed and push through, they suffer (the wielder\u2019s Essence) dice of Initiative damage. Any action that would move a person through the circle (such as a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">disengage </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">rush</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> action) may not be attempted without first succeeding in the Resistance check. If the opponent\u2019s Essence rating is lower than the wielder\u2019s, they cannot avoid this even using magic or other means to bypass the barrier.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inside the circle reality itself holds its breath to witness the duel fought within. The wielder may ignore any wound penalties inflicted before the circle was created and adds a single non-charm bonus die to any </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">clash</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attacks against her opponent for every round passed inside the circle (up to her Essence dice). Additionally, as long as the circle is up neither the wielder nor her opponent reset their Initiative to 3 after a successful </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive attack, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">instead they may reroll Join Battle.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Evocation awakens automatically with no cost, if the wielder meets its prerequisites and suffers a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack from their nemesis that deals more than one Health level of damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Evocation may only be used against an opponent the wielder holds a Major or Defining Tie of rivalry, hatred or any appropriate Intimacy that marks the opponent as the wielder\u2019s nemesis. Even then the Evocation can only be activated once per story, unless the wielder resets it by developing a new Major or Defining Tie towards a different opponent.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Zapatos, the Dancer\u2019s Boots (White Jade Combat boots, 3-dot artifact) </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is a persistent legend of a young Cathak officer, who was kidnapped and enslaved by an Anathema led tyranny. She was stripped of her whole panoply except for her pair of sturdy combat boots the Anathema king let her keep as an insult. For years she was being forced to work in the kingdom\u2019s jade mines among mortal slaves, only to be occasionally brought to the Anathema king\u2019s palace and forced to perform dances and other feats of acrobatics for the king\u2019s amusement. If the Anathema hoped to break the young officer\u2019s spirit, he did not realise how futile it was: for each humiliation and every day in the backbreaking work in the mine only tempered the fire within the young officer\u2019s heart.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still, the Anathema king was cunning and each time the officer planned a rebellion or dug a tunnel to escape through, his demons would spy and uncover such schemes. Until one day the officer stopped struggling: instead she chose to spend her rare free moments dancing.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her dance was so fiery and beautiful that soon other slaves would join her revelry. The Anathema listened to the reports with greater and greater curiosity until his confused servants finally reported everyone in the mines had been caught into the frantic revelry. Eventually the king grew so curious, he had to see it for himself. So he was lead into the mines, where, in his arrogance, he bid his guards to leave as he wanted to observe the dance in peace. For his slaves ignored him in their performance. The king ventured deeper into the mine, fascinated how his rule - for how this could be anything else than his unintended doing? - had given birth to something so beautiful.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thus he marveled until his feet led him to the deepest part of the mine, where the drago- blooded still danced. There the king could not stay silent and spoke: \u201cWhy do you dance my servant? Is it for freedom? Or for joy? I must know!\u201d And the officer listened, her dance stalling only for a moment: \u201cNo. This dance is meant for you and only for you.\u201d</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For a fleeting moment the Anathema king felt pride until the full extent of the officer\u2019s meaning dawned upon him. For right at that moment, the officer and every prisoner descended upon him and engulfed him into their deadly dance - as even when they flowed like water and danced gracefully as the air, their performance had the soul of fire and their moves the strength of the earth. And despite his accursed power, the king could muster no resistance, as every one of his attacks was deflected and bent around like wood.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is said that the former prisoners all saw the Immaculate Dragons\u2019 guidance in the officer\u2019s plans and all flocked under her banner. It is said that they faced countless more adventures before finally returning home. And it is said that they each made a vow to take their secret martial art to their grave. But that is another story.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Zapatos are a pair of combat boots that the officer wore through her long imprisonment. They have since been repaired and reinforced with white jade. It is said that the boots still remember how they defeated the cruel Anathema king and those who wear them become able to wield the secret art developed by the nameless officer.</span></span> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of Zapatos, the Dancer\u2019s Boots</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When attuned the wielder may use their Performance instead of Brawl to attack using the Dancer\u2019s boots or calculate their defenses. Additionally, those resonant with Zapatos may use Performance instead of Stealth to catch an opponent by surprise.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attunement: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5m</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Light artifact weapon</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Worn, Brawl, Lethal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heartstone slots: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Era: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shogunate Era</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thundering Dancer\u2019s Leap</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Zapatos dances, earth beneath tremors in tune with its steps. This evocation supplements a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">disengage</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">rush </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">action. For every 10 on their roll, the wielder may nominate one enemy they were engaged with. That enemy must succeed on a [Dexterity + Athletics) roll against a difficulty of (Wielder\u2019s Essence) or fall prone and suffer an onslaught penalty as if they were attacked by the wielder.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Evocation awakens with no cost when the wielder first attunes to Zapatos, the Dancer\u2019s Boots.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rhythm Poised Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One tick</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those wearing Zapatos can follow the innate rhythm contained within the boots. Opponents cannot help but participate in the wearer\u2019s dance and thus struggle to land a blow. This evocation allows the wearer to ignore up to their Essence in onslaught penalties. Additionally, if they have not moved that turn they may boost their Evasion by their Performance divided by half (round up).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heel Strikes The Face</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous, Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Thundering Dancer\u2019s Leap</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No one can withstand a direct hit from the Dancer\u2019s boots. This evocation supplements a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering or</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack. When making a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering or decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack against a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">prone </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">opponent, the target must apply their onslaught penalty twice. Additionally, if a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive attack</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> deals at least one wound level of damage, the target falls prone (if it wasn\u2019t already) and their onslaught penalty does not reset until they stand up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Turnabout Pirouette</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Heel Strikes the Face</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A foe on the ground is a foe already defeated. This evocation supplements a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack made against a target that\u2019s </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">prone </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or otherwise below the wielder. The wielder may move up to one range band during her attack and may convert (their Essence) damage dice into automatic successes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Quickstep Leap</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Rhythm Poised Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With a graceful twist the Dancer\u2019s boots leap from the ground, striking with lightning speed. This evocation allows the wearer to make an attack against two targets they are engaged with. If this attack is </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, they roll for the attack once and roll damage separately. If the attack is </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">they roll the attack once and then split their Initiative pool between the two targets.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investing the Loyal Chorus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 1 wp Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Heel Strikes Face</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Zapatos\u2019 original owner defeated the Anathema, she did so with the help of her fellow prisoners. The boots still remember the low rumble of its original chorus and seeks to dance again with such backup. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The wielder may activate this evocation to bolster a battlegroup they are leading. The battlegroup must be loyal and familiar to the wielder. (Generally, they must wield an Intimacy towards their commander and/or have been trained personally by the wielder.) As long as the wielder commits the motes and fights alongside the battlegroup, the battlegroup gains +1 Might and Drill, and benefits from the doubled onslaught penalty from Heel Strikes Face. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tremorous Allegro</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous, Withering-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Turnabout Pirouette</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Zapatos drum the ground and the world moves with the beat delivering the wielder\u2019s killing intent against her enemies. This evocation creates a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Dexterity + Brawl OR Performance)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack that targets every </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">prone target </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(up to the maximum of the wielder\u2019s Essence + 1) up to short range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whirlwind Crescendo</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m (1wp) Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Decisive-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Quickstep Leap</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gathering speed from the ground, Zapatos spin upwards in a stirring finale. This evocation creates a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">attack that targets up to the (wielder\u2019s Essence) targets engaged with the wielder. She may roll to hit once and divide her Initiative evenly against every target hit. If the attack also hits a battlegroup, calculate the automatic damage caused by the decisive attack using the wielder\u2019s full Initiative pool.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The wielder may pay a point of Willpower to flung any </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">prone </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">target they hit one range band away. Note that depending on the environment, this might cause more damage from hitting objects or falling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Evocation can only be used once per scene. It can be resetted by causing three or more opponents to fall prone with a single action.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T12:35:14-08:00","id":1278122,"title":"","content":"Oooh. Shiny! Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}